Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: free tx skbs through ieee80211_free_txskb()

ath11k_dp_tx_free_txbuf() drops a data frame with dev_kfree_skb_any(),
which bypasses ieee80211_report_used_skb() and so never returns the
airtime mac80211 charged for the frame on dequeue.

That is harmless today only because ath11k does not advertise
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL, so nothing is ever charged. With the feature bit
set by the next patch, every frame released through this path would leak
its charge: the pending airtime of the access category would rise without
bound and, once it stays above the limit, no station on the radio is
selected in that access category again.

Release the frame through ieee80211_free_txskb() instead, which is what
the other two completion paths in this file already do. The radio pointer
is needed before the release, so look it up first.

This is a backport of patch 1/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
index 562aba6..4cba35e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -303,11 +303,11 @@ static void ath11k_dp_tx_free_txbuf(struct ath11k_base *ab, u8 mac_id,
 	}
 
 	skb_cb = ATH11K_SKB_CB(msdu);
+	ar = ab->pdevs[mac_id].ar;
 
 	dma_unmap_single(ab->dev, skb_cb->paddr, msdu->len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
-	dev_kfree_skb_any(msdu);
+	ieee80211_free_txskb(ar->hw, msdu);
 
-	ar = ab->pdevs[mac_id].ar;
 	if (atomic_dec_and_test(&ar->dp.num_tx_pending))
 		wake_up(&ar->dp.tx_empty_waitq);
 }
